      "text": "To find the new class mean, we need to calculate the total score of all 36 students and then divide by the number of students.\n\nFirst, we calculate the total score of the 30 students who took the test the first time. The mean score of these 30 students is 72%, so the total score for these 30 students is:\n\\[ 30 \\times 72 = 2160 \\]\n\nNext, we calculate the total score of the 6 students who took the test the second time. The mean score of these 6 students is 78%, so the total score for these 6 students is:\n\\[ 6 \\times 78 = 468 \\]\n\nNow, we find the total score of all 36 students by adding the total scores of the two groups:\n\\[ 2160 + 468 = 2628 \\]\n\nThe new class mean is the total score divided by the number of students:\n\\[ \\frac{2628}{36} = 73 \\]\n\nTherefore, the new class mean is:\n\\[ \\boxed{73} \\]",
